<TrustPage title="About TriTimes" description="TriTimes is an independent triathlon results viewer for IRONMAN and IRONMAN 70.3 races, athlete histories, and performance comparisons." canonical="/about">
  <p>TriTimes is an independent triathlon results viewer for IRONMAN and IRONMAN 70.3 races. It helps athletes look beyond a finish time by comparing swim, bike, run, and overall performance with their age group and the full field. You can search for an athlete, explore their race history, browse race editions, and compare courses using finish-time distributions and percentiles.</p>
  <p>Race results come from the Competitor.com results service used by IRONMAN's official results pages. TriTimes organizes those published results for analysis; it does not provide official timing or adjudicate results. Missing splits, names, age groups, and other source errors may also appear here. The <a class="text-link" href="/faq">FAQ</a> explains the data source and its limitations.</p>
  <p>TriTimes is an independent, unofficial project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by The IRONMAN Group or Competitor.com. Race data belongs to its respective owners. The project code is available on <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/rootulp/tritimes">GitHub</a>. To report an issue or ask about the site, visit <a class="text-link" href="/contact">Contact</a>; information about data and browser storage is on the <a class="text-link" href="/privacy">Privacy page</a>.</p>
</TrustPage>
